+---
+
+## Recording expenses
+
+### How do I add an expense?
+
+```
+tally add <amount> <category>
+tally add 12.50 food --note "lunch"
+tally add 39 food --currency EUR --date 2024-03-04
+```
+
+`amount` and `category` are required. `--note`, `--currency`, and `--date` are
+optional. If you omit `--date`, today's date is used.
+
+### What categories can I use?
+
+The built-in categories are:
+
+- `food`
+- `transport`
+- `rent`
+- `entertainment`
+- `other`
+
+Anything outside this list is rejected. To add a custom category, edit
+`KNOWN_CATEGORIES` in `tally/config.py`.
+
+### Can I back-date an expense?
+
+Yes. Pass `--date` in `YYYY-MM-DD` format:
+
+```
+tally add 55 transport --date 2024-02-14
+```
+
+### Can I enter an amount in a foreign currency?
+
+Yes. Pass `--currency` with the currency code, and tally converts it to US
+dollars before saving:
+
+```
+tally add 3500 food --currency JPY
+```
+
+Supported currencies: **EUR, GBP, INR, JPY, SGD, USD**.
+
+The conversion uses fixed rates baked into `tally/rates.py`. Rates are not
+fetched live; they are stable constants you can audit in that file.
+
+### How does currency conversion work exactly?
+
+When you record an expense, the amount is converted to US dollars immediately
+and the dollar figure is what gets stored. The original amount and currency you
+typed are also kept for reference. Every total, report, and export you ever see
+is in US dollars. tally never re-converts at report time, which keeps numbers
+consistent across months that mix currencies.
+
+### What if I recorded something wrong?
+
+Open `tally.json` in any text editor and correct or delete the entry. The file
+is plain JSON — one object per expense. Be careful to keep the JSON valid (no
+trailing commas, matching braces).
+
+---
+
+## Viewing your spending
+
+### How do I see spending for a month?
+
+```
+tally report --month 2024-03
+```
+
+This prints category totals for March 2024. Omit `--month` to see totals across
+all recorded months.
+
+### How do I filter to one category?
+
+```
+tally report --month 2024-03 --category food
+```
+
+Both `report` and `list` accept `--category`.
+
+### How do I list individual expenses instead of totals?
+
+```
+tally list --month 2024-03
+tally list --month 2024-03 --category transport
+```
+
+### How do I see all-time statistics?
+
+```
+tally stats
+```
+
+Prints total number of expenses, grand total in USD, average per expense, and
+the date range covered.
+
+### How do I check spending against my budgets?
+
+```
+tally budget --month 2024-03
+```
+
+Prints each category alongside its configured budget and a status indicator.
+The budgets are defined in `tally/config.py` under `CATEGORY_BUDGETS`. A
+warning appears once spending crosses 80 % of a category's budget.
+
+### How do I export my data to a spreadsheet?
+
+```
+tally export --out march.csv
+```
+
+Writes all expenses as CSV in USD. Omit `--out` to print to standard output.
+
+---
+
+## Plans and backup
+
+### What are the hosted backup plans?
+
+| Plan   | Price        | Expenses per month (backup) | Backup history |
+|--------|--------------|----------------------------|----------------|
+| Free   | $0           | up to 100                  | 7 days         |
+| Plus   | $3 / month   | unlimited                  | 1 year         |
+| Family | $6 / month   | unlimited                  | 3 years        |
+
+Prices are in US dollars, billed monthly.
+
+### How many expenses can I track on the free plan?
+
+There is no local limit — you can record as many expenses as you like. The 100
+per-month cap applies only to which expenses the **hosted backup** covers. If
+you record more than 100 in a month, the extras are saved locally; they are
+just not included in the cloud backup until you upgrade to Plus or Family.
+
+### If I don't use the hosted backup, do any limits apply?
+
+No. Without the backup add-on, tally is entirely local and unlimited.
+
+### Can I upgrade or downgrade my plan?
+
+Yes. Changes take effect at the start of the next billing month.
+
+---
+
+## Data and privacy
+
+### Does tally send my data anywhere?
+
+Not unless you turn on the hosted backup add-on. By default, everything stays
+in the single JSON file on your machine.
+
+### How do I back up or move my data manually?
+
+Copy `tally.json` (or whatever file you specified with `--store`) wherever you
+like. It is plain JSON and self-contained. You can also run `tally export` to
+produce a CSV snapshot.
+
+### Can I use tally on multiple machines?
+
+Yes, but tally has no built-in sync. The simplest approach is to keep the store
+file in a folder that your own sync tool (Dropbox, iCloud Drive, etc.) already
+syncs, and always pass `--store` pointing there. Avoid writing from two machines
+at the same time — the file is not concurrency-safe.
